A manual set four imports deep, for `server import --replace`. manual-sources.tsv
says an earlier import of a file named server-dump.json brought in alpha,
retired and shared, and a Shadowrocket apply brought in shared too; byhand has
no line (added with `server add`).

Re-importing tests/parity/fixtures/server-dump.json (alpha, gamma) with
--replace must drop alpha and retired, keep shared (another source still
claims it) and byhand (no source), add alpha and gamma back, and record
file:server-dump.json -> alpha, gamma beside shadowrocket -> shared. Without
--replace nothing is dropped. `server rm retired` and `server clear` must prune
the lines of the servers they remove.
